WEBVTT

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:03.500
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.460
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.940
My name is Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.620
I'm a first-year middle school student

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.060
who's currently attending the idol training school Starlight Academy with my best friend Aoi.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.460
Aikatsu stands for "idol activities", which include applying for auditions and getting gigs.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.350
We use Aikatsu cards to choose our own outfits and stages.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:30.000
My last audition was for a fashion show,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.510
and moreover it was a team audition with Ran-chan!

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.900
She was a bit scary at first,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.510
but that was just because of how seriously she took her modeling and idol work.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.270
We somehow managed to pass the audition.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:45.760
Now we've got our magazine 
modeling job, and I'm getting nervous!

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:48.870
Please excuse us.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.990
Wow!

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:54.520
Isn't it amazing, Ran-chan?

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.440
Don't call me that!

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:58.220
And calm down, it's unbecoming.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.720
But we're about to be in a 
photo shoot. I can't help it!

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.020
We managed to get the job, after all.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.000
Let's do our best, Ran-chan.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.380
And there goes the tension...

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.500
Shibuki-san, Hoshimiya-san!

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.010
Wh-What is it?

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.220
A gift for the readers. One more please.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.160
Thanks!

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:24.820
I'm looking forward to working with you today.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.100
Same here. Could you sign these and wait a bit?

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:28.980
Sure.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:29.900
What's that?

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.260
Haven't you seen it in the back of magazines?

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.400
They give away autographed photos.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.520
Wow, your signature's so cool!

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.720
You want me to sign it too?

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:54.340
Is this your first time signing something?

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.550
What should I do?

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.000
I don't have a signature!

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.390
Hi, signalize!

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:22.730
The answer lies on the other side of the sky

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:22.730
kotae wa motto takai sora no kanata

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.620
No, that's wrong

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:24.620
iie chigau yo

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:30.000
I can see with my eyes that it's at the end of the Earth

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:30.000
boku no me ni mo mieta chi no hate

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.790
Do that signalize!

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.970
Something's starting to bubble up

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.970
hageshiku natta mune no atsui powaa

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.930
From the burning power in my raging heart

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:40.930
sou da minagiru nanika ga

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.470
So I'll believe in the present

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.470
dakara ima wo shinjite

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.640
And start today since it's more than a faint desire

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.640
hajimeyou tada no akogare ja nai

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:50.980
Chance for me

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:56.280
Dreams can make even the harshest nightmare pleasant

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:56.280
zankoku na yume ga yume de yume ni narunda

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.490
It's just another challenge on the way

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.490
hora chousen matteru yo

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.410
Where are we headed?

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.410
kimi to mukau basho wa doko darou

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.160
Into a brilliant hope

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.160
mabushii kibou no nake e

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:16.420
Where do we want to go? Let's go find it right now

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:16.420
nozomu basho wa doko darou sagashi ni ikou yo shuppatsu da

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.800
Where we're headed

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.800
mukau basho wa mirai no

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.680
is into our hopes for the future

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.680
bokura no kibou no naka ni

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:31.020
Our destination is the future, the light is our signal Let's go, go!

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:31.020
nozomu basho wa mirai no kagayaki ga aizu let's go, go

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.610
Ran's great as usual! Every pose is perfect.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.800
I can still see stars in my eyes.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.380
So how was the shoot?

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:48.700
They got mad at me.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.180
With a bit more languor...

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.980
Right, perfect!

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.380
Now why don't we have Hoshimiya-san join you?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:03:58.880
Y-Yes!

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.890
Act more like yourself.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.600
Like myself?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.060
Hoshimiya, this isn't some sort of photo booth.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:20.900
Even though the two of you passed together, this is more like Ran with a side of Ichigo.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.000
"A side"?

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.220
For example, Ran would be curry, and you would be leek.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.040
But I want to be the hard-boiled egg!

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.420
But leeks are so yummy! Ah, there's writing.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.840
Ah, that. I practiced my signature.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.420
Signature?

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:34.920
Bad, <i>bad,</i> <i>BAD!</i>

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.110
Sensei!

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.420
You call this a signature?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.430
It's nothing! Why?

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.930
There's no way I could've thought of a signature that fast.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:51.180
Honey, how can you call yourself an idol if you don't have an autograph?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.560
I just don't have one.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.180
Me neither.

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.810
Mistake!

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:01.060
I forgot to tell you two honeys to prepare an autograph after you transferred in.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.160
I'm sorry, honeys. I'm so useless.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:05.340
Sensei...

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.580
Then here's your homework: design an autograph.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.600
Due date's tomorrow.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.280
Tomorrow?!

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.640
Yes, tomorrow!

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.660
Um, any advice on making it?

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.260
Inspiration is the most important thing.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:20.210
I'm expecting a fresh and sweet autograph from you.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.620
An autograph, huh...

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.540
Hey, what do you think of these?

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.720
You already thought of one?

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:36.300
How about like this?

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.680
It's from when Shio-tan was a child actor.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.200
This one's cute too!

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:44.800
Haruru, huh? Her agency basically forbid autographs,

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.920
so it's said that you have to use up all the luck in your life to get your hands on it.

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.360
I see.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.620
First we need to pick some sort of direction.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.440
Drawing something like a flower or a heart really makes it cuter.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:58.450
And on top of that,

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:03.130
the impression it gives off changes depending on whether you use hiragana, katakana, kanji, or romaji.

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.340
Have you decided on anything yet?

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:08.180
Well, something cute and cool,

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.240
and awesome too!

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.880
So you've got no idea.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.600
I don't even know where to begin...

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:25.180
Ran!

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.240
Ran-chan!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.360
I refuse!

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.160
We haven't even said anything yet.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.460
About your signature, right?

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:31.620
Exactly!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.190
I want to get a knowledgeable opinion.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.160
Please teach us how to make one!

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.340
Why does it have to be me? Go ask someone else.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.930
Your signature was really cool!

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.340
I want to have a signature like that too!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.500
Ran-chan, please! Help me out!

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.420
I told you not to call me that!

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.900
Sorry...

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.020
Fine...

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.660
I'll give you a hand.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.440
Ran-chan!

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:04.900
I'm coming in.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.260
Welcome!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.160
Are we a shop?

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.240
The preorder gift for her first album, huh.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:17.360
You know about it? I lost net connection right when the mail-order site went online.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.560
I finally connected after 10 minutes, but they were already sold out,

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:25.840
so I cried all the way to the local CD shop, and when I showed them my preorder ticket I was finally able to get my poster!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.060
Was it the same for you?

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.900
I <i>do</i> have it but I didn't cry to reserve it.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.180
So you like Mizuki-chan too!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.220
What of it?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.460
We're the same!

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.470
Sure, sure.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.580
Now we just need drinks and snacks.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:44.560
Aren't you going to change?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.340
We couldn't be the only ones relaxing...

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:48.320
Yeah.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.070
There's no need to worry, I'm leaving soon.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:51.820
You're gonna leave?

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.610
Don't leave us!

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:55.220
You'll crease my clothes!

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:58.560
Fine, I'll get changed and come back.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.670
Geez, why do I have to...

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.420
Welcome home!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.160
...I'm back.

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:11.600
Casual clothes are great! That rough feeling makes you even more sexy! Now this is rare.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.740
Please refrain from taking pictures or recording video.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.430
I brought some snacks with me too.

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.260
"Snacks"...

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.430
So simple!

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:25.220
As I thought! You don't spoil yourself even when eating snacks!

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.440
Well, even I sometimes do...

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.520
It really is simple!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.900
First, write your name several times.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.100
Understood!

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:38.180
Kanji, hiragana, katakana, and cursive romaji.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:39.000
Cursive?

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.160
You're starting there?!

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:43.680
Wow, it looks real!

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.160
Maybe I'll use romaji...

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:49.020
Kanji feels kind of stiff, and it seems like it'll be hard.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.380
I think it's fine to be distinctive,

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:54.820
but if you think it's too stiff then you can shorten it.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.080
Try writing with more curves.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:58.390
It feels like an autograph!

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:01.520
Good start. Try and figure out the rest yourself.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.120
Right!

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.940
Ran-chan, what about me?

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.190
What style?

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.900
I'll use cursive!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.940
Then write it 50 times. Thinking about the arrangement comes after.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:14.040
Write until your hand remembers!

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.160
Tell me when you're done; I'm going to organize my cards.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.800
There are so many Aikatsu cards!

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.200
And there are rare ones too!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:32.920
"Rare"?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.840
Cards with a lot of appeal points. Brand name items really are strong!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.930
I really like the Angely Sugar brand.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:44.560
The lace and ribbons are so floaty.
 I'm overjoyed just thinking about it!

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:45.480
Hoshimiya.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.940
Sign an additional 50 times!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.940
Why is it just me?

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.400
Nice job.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:57.800
I'm confident about it!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.950
Take a look at my autograph! Isn't it cute?

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.340
Whoa!

00:10:04.340 --> 00:10:05.440
You tried too hard.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.160
I used all my effort! Well, well?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.480
It seems hard to write, but if you like it then isn't that enough?

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:15.000
Yay, I'm done!

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:18.400
Wanna go to the cafeteria?

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.930
Yeah. I thought so much that my stomach's hit its limit.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:23.220
Then I'll head back.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.720
Aren't you going to eat?

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.590
I never eat anything after 8 at night.

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:29.760
Sorry, I didn't realize it was that late.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.480
I filled myself on the snacks so don't worry about it.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:34.440
Thanks a bunch, Ran-chan.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.000
You really saved us.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.740
No problem. I also had fu—

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.000
Good night.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:50.940
Moe...

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:51.960
Moe?

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:55.620
How embarrassing...

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:00.420
I'll send it to Raichi too.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.700
We made some good ones thanks to Ran.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.740
I bet Sensei'll be surprised too.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:07.440
Oh, a special cute autograph!

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:09.180
Is that an impression?

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:12.500
Miracle cosmic cutie!

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.500
That makes no sense!

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.700
Cool!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:23.330
And charming! Nice autograph.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.620
Thank you very much!

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:28.660
Be sure to practice so that you can write it anytime, anywhere.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.460
Practice and practice!

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.660
Understand?

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.380
Yes.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.440
Next.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:35.920
Please take a look.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.120
Poison. Destroy.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.930
Is it that bad?

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:48.380
No. It's very, very, very sweet...

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.890
But <i>heavy</i>.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:50.880
Heavy?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:51.940
Like, weight?

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.190
How long do you think it'll take to write this?

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.860
Um...

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.900
Adieu. Try again.

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.700
If you take your sweet time signing, your fans will start leaving, baby.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.940
What's important is speed and love.

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:09.680
Got it.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:10.900
Are you gonna make a new one?

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.540
Nope. I'm not gonna change it.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:14.960
I'm just going to train.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.320
Are you going to start an autograph booth or something?

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:35.960
It's for the training.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:44.070
Aikatsu... Aikatsu...

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.820
What's she doing?

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:51.070
Training to improve her signing speed.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:54.500
Aikatsu... Ai...

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:58.880
Ow...

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:06.800
Ai... katsu...

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.350
A little bigger! And you're leaning too far right!

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.960
Is she ever going to need to sign something that big?

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.240
You'd better drill that autograph into your soul!

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:18.920
Aikatsu. Aikatsu.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:19.690
Done!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.900
Too slow.

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:27.660
Aikatsu. Aikatsu.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.300
Done! Done! Done!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.900
Did I get under 20 seconds this time?

00:13:35.490 --> 00:13:36.290
It's a repdigit.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.340
I can't break the 20 second barrier.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:39.820
You're already good enough, I think.

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:43.300
Nope, my goal is ten seconds! One more time!

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:47.800
Ten seconds exactly.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:50.820
Yay!

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.060
Good job.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.160
You did great today.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.000
Thanks, you two.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.380
Hey, can I try signing something for you two?

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.500
Sure, but...

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:00.780
Doesn't your hand hurt?

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:05.320
Not at all! I want to keep signing things until I drop!

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.080
Ichigo's on fire.

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:11.740
Hoshimiya-san, there's a package for you in the hallway.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.710
Oh, you're the street-sweeping guy. {intenionally leaving it like this just this once}

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.020
Thank you very much for helping me back there.

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:27.760
It was nothing. Here, a package for you.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.020
Yay! Mandarins!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.520
<b>Onee-chan
 Aoi-neesan</b>

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.000
Want some?

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:39.900
My nails will turn yellow, so no thanks.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:44.660
So Raichi said that everyone from the shopping district wanted to see us.

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:45.530
Really?

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.030
Let's go then! Tomorrow's Sunday, too.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.180
Tomorrow?

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.160
Ran-chan should come too.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.000
Me?

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.020
You should try our seaweed bento.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.540
Seaweed bento...

00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.790
Onee-chan and company are here!

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.160
Huh? In front of Ichigo's house...

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.040
We have so many customers...

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.300
I guess business is good.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.740
Look.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:11.320
Autograph session?

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.540
Welcome home, Ichigo-chan!

00:15:13.540 --> 00:15:15.280
Whoa! It's Aoi-chan!

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.080
And is that Shibuki Ran?!

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.060
Calm down, everyone.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:21.850
Welcome home!

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:23.690
Hey, Raichi!

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:27.030
You never told me about this autograph session thing!

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.260
Well, since you said you'd come...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.280
Sorry, I had no idea.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.980
Geez, don't do that.

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:35.030
We meet with such misfortune.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:38.680
Shibuki Ran-san?

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:39.780
The real one?

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:41.920
Why's she here?

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.170
Is something wrong with that?

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.220
She's for real!

00:15:45.850 --> 00:15:48.680
What do we do? Looks like there are people who came quite a way to see us.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.040
I guess we'll have to do it.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.700
We've trained for this, after all.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.200
Okay!

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:53.180
Then...

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.680
Ran-chan!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.840
Hold on a minute.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.680
Numbers up through 20, step up.

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:10.940
Have some if you'd like.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:14.950
I'm sure you're helping Ichigo out with all sorts of things.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.400
Ah, I learn from her too.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.450
What do you think of those girls?

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.440
Aoi-chan, who's your favorite idol?

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:25.960
There're some that've caught my interest lately, but it's definitely Mizuki-san.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.710
Nice to meet you, um...

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:31.220
I became a fan after seeing your video on the internet, and...

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.220
Ichigo-chan?

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.280
Done! Here.

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:37.220
Oh. Thanks.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.720
Okay, then. I'll be cheering you on.

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.180
This, please.

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:45.180
Okay!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.260
Um...

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.990
Done! Here.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.320
Huh? Ran-chan?

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.000
Who are you signing for?

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.240
Who...

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.140
They saw the way you treated your fans and left.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.000
Huh? Did I make them wait too long?

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.430
No. They feel let down.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.560
You were great at your last audition.

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:23.080
Thank you very much.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.810
Keep at it.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.760
Why do you think your fans are here?

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:30.480
They're not here because they wanted your autograph.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.280
They wanted to meet you.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:36.020
And yet, you just signed those cards without ever looking up at your fans.

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.910
Would anyone want an autograph from someone like that?

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:43.220
I was lost in writing my autograph.

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:44.330
Um...

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:48.160
Hoshimiya Ichigo-san, are you still signing autographs?

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.040
Ah, yes!

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.260
Keep your head up like that.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.460
It's fine if your autograph turns out a little messy.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:57.050
Okay!

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:01.380
Stop, honey.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.480
Are you a light-speed autographer yet?

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.660
Yes. Oh, but...

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.400
Let me see.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:10.900
Um... so, what's your name?

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.820
Me? Johnny.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.700
Johnny-san. Where did you come from today?

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.100
Top secret!

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:20.200
Sensei, you're just full of mysteries, aren't you? Were you always like that?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.660
Top secret.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.420
Then, what do you eat for breakfast? Rice or bread?

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:25.340
Ri—

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:27.480
Rye? Like rye bread?

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:29.580
Rice. Like, you know, rice.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:30.670
I see!

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.670
Ah, it turned out all over the place.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.440
Sorry.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.240
Yes! Well done!

00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:44.430
You fought your heavy sign and won.

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.960
Honey, your talk was thrilling good!

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.440
Yay!

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:51.440
A present for your hard work.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:54.540
{Wow! }Angely Sugar!

00:18:54.540 --> 00:18:56.190
They're rare cards. Yeah!

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:59.210
They're so cute! Thank you very much!

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:03.340
There's an audition that'd be perfect for you. Wanna give it a try?

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:06.950
If you pass, you'll be an image character for a brand of stationery.

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:09.460
Please, sign me up!

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.360
<i>I can't believe I forgot.</i>

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:17.220
<i>That every customer should be treated with care.</i>

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:20.660
<i>And that more important than the 
autographs are the people who want them.</i>

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:23.380
Next up, Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:24.460
Yes!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:33.940
<i>In order to make the people I let down want to come see me again,</i>

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.480
<i>I will give it my all!</i>

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:30.240
Our eyes on the goal

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:54.020
Nice to meet you, everyone. I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:57.870
We're announcing the launch of a new seven-colored feelings-conveying felt-tip pen!

00:21:57.870 --> 00:22:00.880
Dye your notebooks and letters in your very own color!

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:03.480
I can't believe you came.

00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:05.380
I didn't come because I was worried about her or anything.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.680
I just wanted to put pressure on her.

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:13.380
Look at this! It writes so clearly, too!

00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:15.390
See?

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:18.380
Wait, that's just because you trained for it!

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:21.940
Give it a try!

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:57.800
Ichigo, why don't you try using microblogging?

00:23:57.800 --> 00:23:58.320
Huh?

00:23:58.320 --> 00:24:01.700
KiraKiratter. It's where all the cool people microblog.

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:03.940
I've gotta post a lot too!

00:24:03.940 --> 00:24:05.420
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:07.020
Beware the Blog.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:10.320
Always passionate, Idol Activities!

00:24:11.210 --> 00:24:13.130
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:24:14.170 --> 00:24:14.910
Done!

00:24:14.910 --> 00:24:16.690
Amazing! That was under 10 seconds.

00:24:16.690 --> 00:24:18.730
Signing quickly just doesn't seem like enough.

00:24:18.730 --> 00:24:20.470
Next I'll try to write with my eyes closed!

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:21.930
I think you're missing the point.

00:24:21.930 --> 00:24:22.970
Aphorism time.

00:24:23.630 --> 00:24:25.270
Look forward while you sign!
